# Shell scripts must reach Android/Termux with LF endings. A CRLF shebang line
# fails as `bad interpreter: /data/data/.../bash^M`, which reads like a missing
# interpreter rather than a line-ending problem and wastes an hour every time.
# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, so the guard is
# not theoretical.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Purpose-contract evidence hashes bind to committed bytes. Keep evidence-bearing
# text stable across Linux and Windows checkouts so core.autocrlf cannot rewrite
# an authoritative file after its owner-observed SHA-256 was recorded.
*.py text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.java text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
